    question: "How much internet speed does VoIP actually need?",
    answer:
      "Surprisingly little — roughly 100 kbps per concurrent call. Ten simultaneous calls need about 1 Mbps, which any business NBN plan handles easily. Call quality problems are almost never about raw speed; they're about congestion and jitter, which is why a router with quality-of-service (QoS) settings matters more than a faster plan.",
  },
