    question: "What happens to VoIP phones during a power or internet outage?",
    answer:
      "Desk phones go down with the power or the connection — but modern VoIP fails over gracefully: calls can automatically redirect to mobiles, another site, or voicemail-to-email. With a 4G/5G backup link on your router, most outages become invisible to callers. A landline-era system in a blackout just rings out.",
  },
  {
    question: "Is VoIP call quality really as good as a landline?",
    answer:
      "On a properly configured connection, yes — typically better, since VoIP supports HD voice codecs that traditional copper lines never could. The qualifier matters: VoIP on congested, unmanaged internet can sound bad. Set up correctly, your callers won't be able to tell, except that it sounds clearer.",
